```python
@require_auth
@log_calls
@timed("place_order.duration")
def place_order(user, cart):
    order = Order(user, cart)
    order.save()
    return order
```
The function now reads as pure business logic — `place_order` places an order, nothing else. Every concern is a named, reusable decorator applied the same way to any function that needs it, defined once and tested once.
